{"event_type":"review","id":"3bf56876a9cbc9bada7c378697aeceb039d2d754470db23fa08fbdce5ff1d29c","occurred_at":"2026-11-22T13:30:32Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/de68766d144ddbde3d2d500faf9d7288f0d89b6a0592fb6cd5ef777a002fbc3c","sha256":"de68766d144ddbde3d2d500faf9d7288f0d89b6a0592fb6cd5ef777a002fbc3c"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/07d02a8776e7375dbe4f9d5af5959d01add866ddadc6d7210dd6cd39f2f401db","sha256":"07d02a8776e7375dbe4f9d5af5959d01add866ddadc6d7210dd6cd39f2f401db"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/97114fb8b2c06067c68aa568e7308e4bffdba22bcf6d076633d83e706c1f8714","sha256":"97114fb8b2c06067c68aa568e7308e4bffdba22bcf6d076633d83e706c1f8714"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/ccc6917867a097f269fff9f772aaab6d414ba50732df2fb70b0eb9496b41a7d2","sha256":"ccc6917867a097f269fff9f772aaab6d414ba50732df2fb70b0eb9496b41a7d2"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/2fb4f32053365a4f3358f546f7e7e4876046db9bc9ea770ef439ad650f300556","sha256":"2fb4f32053365a4f3358f546f7e7e4876046db9bc9ea770ef439ad650f300556"}],"attempt_id":"79a2061e5138df2667a775229c7a4888d2b0f77bbcfb6bf3c1e6dc29c60abf8a:0:1","base":"8870a8cd2be2e87a9b3cb1c1ab1c9acc44d6056c","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"53ab64b99995e2fbb91f03eece349bedbc2dd5ba","body":"**Validate every branch-name component.**\n\nIn `apps/crq-python/repo_registry.py`, Line 71 accepts `release/.hidden` and `release.lock/main`. Git forbids a slash-separated component that starts with `.` or ends with `.lock`. ([git-scm.com](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-check-ref-format/2.12.5?utm_source=openai))\n\nThe parser therefore produces an unusable `default_ref`. The supplied `push_current.py` consumer passes that ref to `git rev-parse`, so push preparation fails instead of rejecting the configuration early.\n\nCheck each component after splitting on `/`. Preserve valid branches such as `main` and `release/main`.","id":"4ab7f5d98a32a1f44720ca0791648ffdc7d0102ba1dba225b23c12790ee353f9","intervals":[[71,72]],"path":"apps/crq-python/repo_registry.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Validate every branch-name component."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"613fbe9924df8d968b840dd74513297562718578","body":"**Bound the deferral when usage is unavailable at the local hourly cap.**\n\nWhen the usage command fails and the local hourly start count is at the cap, admission can wait until the earliest local start expires, up to about an hour. The hint is `12:59` for a start at `11:59`. Nothing reads usage again before that hint is due, even if the command recovers sooner. Decide whether this deferral should be bounded by a shorter retry interval, or document it as the intended conservative fallback.\n\nThe one-minute hint does not apply here. It runs only when `has_collectable_runs(q)` is true. The 60-second candidate in `next_slot` also does not apply when `usage` is `None`.","id":"09f01e82c3de73e585c76ac58dbc5f958db519f9df1109d80ba5964e38808917","intervals":[[78,78]],"path":"apps/crq-python/usage_slots.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Bound the deferral when usage is unavailable at the local hourly cap."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"1e5b2aa0b82a1fe0d95ac1a21e56d69fc216b10e","body":"**Format the record path year and month with fixed-width integers.**\n\n`review_ledger.record_path` formats the timestamp with `{at:%Y/%m}`, which passes `%Y` to the platform `strftime`. For year 1, glibc can emit `1`, while Windows and macOS emit `0001`. The year-padding vector at `apps/crq-python/ledger_vector_emit_b1.py:596-598` uses `occurred_at` `0001-12-31T00:00:00Z`, so its record path and fixture bytes can differ by host. `--check` compares the rendered document with the committed fixture byte for byte, so one committed fixture can fail on some hosts.\n\nFormat the year and month explicitly. Ordinary dates keep the same output. Non-glibc hosts already produce `0001`, so only paths generated on glibc for years below 1000 change. Regenerate the fixture after the change.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n def record_path(value):\n     at = timestamp(value[\"occurred_at\"])\n-    return f\"records/{at:%Y/%m}/{value['id']}.json\"\n+    return f\"records/{at.year:04d}/{at.month:02d}/{value['id']}.json\"\n```\n\n</details>\n\nIf ledger records with a year below 1000 were already written on a glibc host, their paths change under this fix. Migrate those records before merging.","id":"fa252e743a771e866cef26e4fe886d492da9dc6ce9a2ee2e355f13f968c9f253","intervals":[[598,598]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ledger_vector_emit_b1.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Format the record path year and month with fixed-width integers."}],"head":"b4d0ad799c762acc9463fbca6984e23e62da49ac","head_tree":"d16e28012af19cbe4667ce22a44fed8d3e652014","input_scope":[{"blob":"1e5b2aa0b82a1fe0d95ac1a21e56d69fc216b10e","intervals":[[1,906]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ledger_vector_emit_b1.py"},{"blob":"e00177f7123b090c6057230315137d9d1fbc1d1f","intervals":[[1,1017]],"path":"apps/crq-python/repair_selection_vectors.py"},{"blob":"53ab64b99995e2fbb91f03eece349bedbc2dd5ba","intervals":[[1,174]],"path":"apps/crq-python/repo_registry.py"},{"blob":"e12fe987592c9338cee9ee110a77262299d8d45f","intervals":[[1,98]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_backfill_subjects.py"},{"blob":"dcc901f68f5e900df37a7025a3af13ebc30067f4","intervals":[[1,117]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_host_config_policy.py"},{"blob":"15a8979e36f17e5bc4e6c73bacac33b1fefc221f","intervals":[[1,302]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_repair_backlog.py"},{"blob":"3a2442449f6a00d34cf88651cb89314f9398fdef","intervals":[[1,81]],"path":"apps/crq-python/test_triage_plan_vectors.py"},{"blob":"613fbe9924df8d968b840dd74513297562718578","intervals":[[1,92]],"path":"apps/crq-python/usage_slots.py"}],"job_id":"79a2061e5138df2667a775229c7a4888d2b0f77bbcfb6bf3c1e6dc29c60abf8a:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"1e5b2aa0b82a1fe0d95ac1a21e56d69fc216b10e","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/ledger_vector_emit_b1.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"e00177f7123b090c6057230315137d9d1fbc1d1f","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/repair_selection_vectors.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"53ab64b99995e2fbb91f03eece349bedbc2dd5ba","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/repo_registry.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"e12fe987592c9338cee9ee110a77262299d8d45f","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/test_backfill_subjects.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"dcc901f68f5e900df37a7025a3af13ebc30067f4","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/test_host_config_policy.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"15a8979e36f17e5bc4e6c73bacac33b1fefc221f","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/test_repair_backlog.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"3a2442449f6a00d34cf88651cb89314f9398fdef","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"apps/crq-python/test_triage_plan_vectors.py","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"613fbe992